   $q$Team Red scored 10, 12, 14, 16, 18 points in five games. Team Blue scored 4, 9, 14, 19, 24 points. Which statement is true?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Both teams have a mean of 14, but Team Red's scores are more spread out.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reversed-the-spread"},{"text":"Team Blue has a higher mean because it has the highest single score.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"extreme-value-as-center"},{"text":"Both teams have a mean of 14, but Team Blue's scores are more spread out.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Both teams have the same mean, so they also have the same range.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"same-center-means-same-spread"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Both teams have a mean of 14, but Team Blue's scores are more spread out.$q$, $q$Each team's scores add to 70, so both means are $70 \div 5 = 14$, but Team Blue's range is $24 - 4 = 20$ while Team Red's is $18 - 10 = 8$. Having the same mean does not make the spreads the same.$q$, 'draft', null)
