   $q$Fifteen students reported how many times they visited a museum this year. 0 visits: 6 students, 1 visit: 2 students, 2 visits: 2 students, 3 visits: 3 students, 4 visits: 2 students. What is the median number of visits?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$2$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"took-middle-of-categories"},{"text":"$4$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"found-the-range"},{"text":"$0$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"gave-the-mode"},{"text":"$1$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$1$$q$, $q$With 15 values the median is the 8th in order; the first 6 values are 0 and the 7th and 8th are 1, so the median is 1. The choice $2$ is the middle of the list 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, which ignores how many students gave each answer.$q$, 'draft', null)
