   $q$Set P is 2, 3, 5, 6, 8, 9. Set R is 1, 4, 5, 6, 7, 15. Which statement is true?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Set P has the greater range and the greater IQR.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reversed-the-range"},{"text":"The two sets have the same IQR.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"computed-quartiles-wrong"},{"text":"Set R has the greater range and the greater IQR.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"assumed-range-predicts-iqr"},{"text":"Set R has the greater range, but Set P has the greater IQR.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Set R has the greater range, but Set P has the greater IQR.$q$, $q$Set P has range $9 - 2 = 7$ and IQR $8 - 3 = 5$, while Set R has range $15 - 1 = 14$ and IQR $7 - 4 = 3$. A large range in Set R comes from its extreme values, which the IQR ignores.$q$, 'draft', null)
