   $q$The data set 4, 6, x, 11, 13, 16 is in order from least to greatest, and its median is 10. What is the value of x?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$20$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"forgot-to-subtract"},{"text":"$9$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$10$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"median-must-be-a-data-value"},{"text":"$1$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"subtracted-from-neighbor"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$9$$q$, $q$With six values the median is the mean of the third and fourth values, so $\frac{x + 11}{2} = 10$, which means $x + 11 = 20$ and $x = 9$. The choice $10$ assumes the median must be one of the data values, but here it is halfway between x and 11.$q$, 'draft', null)
