   $q$Jun asked 20 classmates, "How many letters are in your first name?" The answers ranged from 3 to 9. Which statement is true?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It became statistical only after Jun found the mean.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"calculation-makes-statistical"},{"text":"It is not statistical, because the answers are whole numbers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"number-type-decides-statistical"},{"text":"It is statistical, because Jun expects the answers to vary.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It is not statistical, because each person has only one answer.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"each-person-one-answer"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It is statistical, because Jun expects the answers to vary.$q$, $q$The question is asked of a group and the answers vary from 3 to 9, so it is a statistical question. Each person giving one answer does not matter, since the variety across the whole group is what counts.$q$, 'draft', null)
